.coverage
htmlcov/

# LACC: local user data must never be committed
# Configurations. Anything at the root whose name starts with `config` is ignored,
# and the template is re-included by name. Matching the shape rather than the exact
# filename is deliberate: the first person to follow the guide saved theirs as
# `config.yaml.txt`, which a rule naming only `config.yaml` would have missed - and it
# held a live ntfy token. A rule that catches only the spelling you predicted is a rule
# that catches nothing you did not.
#
# The configs/ folder is ignored in full, never a mix of tracked and untracked files:
# a folder where some configurations are committed and others are not is how a private
# one eventually gets committed by someone filling in the wrong file.
/config*
!/config.example.yaml
/workspaces/
/.local_workspaces/
*.local.yaml
.env
.env.*
/lacc-workspace/
*.jsonl

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Scratch file used for manual provider testing
notas.txt